# Docker build-context hygiene.
# The Dockerfile copies sources and rebuilds node_modules/dist inside the image
# (RUN rm -R ...), so those do not belong in the build context. Without this file
# the multi-GB *.tar image exports would be sent as context and bloat every build.

# Dependencies & build artifacts (rebuilt fresh inside the image)
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Native addon build output (the clusterquic Rust addon is rebuilt inside the
# image; its Cargo target/ and *.node prebuilds are huge and must not be sent
# as build context)
clusterquic/target
clusterquic/*.node
clusterquic/index.js
clusterquic/index.d.ts
clustertun/target
clustertun/*.node
clustertun/index.js
clustertun/index.d.ts

# Local image exports (multiple GB) - never needed in the build context
*.tar

# VCS / IDE / CI
.git
.gitignore
.github
.idea
.vscode

# Docs & design artifacts
doc
*.pdf
flyingfish.spdx.json

# Local / runtime data
.env
**/*.log
nginx/logs
nginx/servers
nginx/sample
nginx/body
nginxtest
letsencrypt

# Misc
.mcp.json
.claude
